00:40:25,000 --> 00:40:31,000
Janis Lyn Joplin (January 19, 1943 – October 4, 1970)
was an American singer and songwriter.

11
00:44:27,500 --> 00:44:33,500
One of the most iconic and successful rock performers of her era, she was noted for
her powerful mezzo-soprano vocals and her "electric" stage presence.

12
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:36,000
In 1967, Joplin rose to prominence following an appearance at the Monterey Pop Festival, where she was the lead
singer of the then little-known San Francisco psychedelic rock band Big Brother and the Holding Company.

13
00:52:32,500 --> 00:52:38,500
After releasing two albums with the band, she left Big Brother to continue as a solo artist with her
own backing groups, first the Kozmic Blues Band and then the Full Tilt Boogie Band.

14
00:56:35,000 --> 00:56:41,000
She performed at the 1969 Woodstock Festival and on
the Festival Express train tour.

15
01:00:37,500 --> 01:00:43,500
Five singles by Joplin reached the US Billboard Hot 100, including a cover of the Kris
Kristofferson song "Me and Bobby McGee", which posthumously reached number one in March 1971.

16
01:04:40,000 --> 01:04:46,000
Her most popular songs include her cover versions of "Piece of My Heart", "Cry Baby", "Down on Me", "Ball and
Chain", and "Summertime", as well as her original song "Mercedes Benz", which was her final recording.

17
01:08:42,500 --> 01:08:48,500
Joplin died of a heroin overdose in 1970, at the age of 27, after releasing three
albums (two with Big Brother and the Holding Company and one solo album).

18
01:12:45,000 --> 01:12:51,000
A second solo album, Pearl, was released in January
1971, three months after her death.

19
01:16:47,500 --> 01:16:53,500
It reached number one on the Billboard 200.

20
01:20:50,000 --> 01:20:56,000
She was posthumously inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame in 1995.

21
01:24:52,500 --> 01:24:58,500
Rolling Stone ranked Joplin  number 28 on its 2008 list of the "200 Greatest
Singers of All Time", dropping to number 78 in the 2023 list.

22
01:28:55,000 --> 01:29:01,000
As of 2013, she remains one of the top-selling vocalists in the United States, with Recording
Industry Association of America (RIAA) certifications of 18.5 million albums sold.

23
01:32:57,500 --> 01:33:03,500
The film explores themes of movie business, stuntman,
swimming pool, hot tub, special effects.
